        "original_id": "d9bef0c9-8e52-58b8-a454-d0675147b03f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Christian Friedrich Schönbein, William Robert Grove, Robert Cumming\n- Roles: Chemists, Judges, Physical Scientists\n- Products: Fuel cell, Guncotton, Ozone\n- Concepts: Conservation of energy\n\nFacts:\n- Christian Friedrich Schönbein was a German-Swiss chemist who lived from 18 October 1799 to 29 August 1868.\n- In 1838, Christian Friedrich Schönbein invented the fuel cell at the same time as William Robert Grove and Robert Cumming.\n- Christian Friedrich Schönbein is also known for his discoveries of guncotton and ozone.\n- William Robert Grove was a Welsh judge and physical scientist who lived from 11 July 1811 to 1 August 1896.\n- William Robert Grove anticipated the general theory of the conservation of energy.\n- William Robert Grove was a pioneer of fuel cell technology.",
